IMPORT prelude

-- Boy Scouts Association Act 1926 (Singapore) -- who is a "boy scout" (s 2), selling scout badges (s 3), wearing them without being a
-- scout (s 4), a scout using a badge to exercise authority (s 5), forming or working with an unauthorised "boy scouts" body (s 6), and
-- the penalty (s 7). That is every operative section of the Act.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSAA1926.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its legislative history lists only one
-- amending law after the 1926 Ordinance: Ordinance 37 of 1952, the Law Revision (Penalties Amendment) Ordinance (in force 30 April 1955);
-- the rest are revised editions (1936, 1955, 1970, 1985, 2011).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0228 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- Act is seven sections long, so nothing operative is left out. Not encoded: the short title (s 1); what the Association's
-- constitution, by-laws and rules say -- who is recognised as a boy scout, which badges are "specifically adopted", and what authority a
-- scout may exercise. Those are the Association's own documents and none is in the deposit; this encoding takes each as a fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Boy Scouts Association Act 1926 -- badges and the name`

-- One record describes a person and what the person did. Each flag is a fact the Act takes from outside itself or from the conduct.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `is the Association itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is recognised as a boy scout under the Association's rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an officer of the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sold or exposed for sale the item` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the item is a badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for boy scouts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the item only purports or appears to be an Association badge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publicly wore, carried or bore the item` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a manner conveying the impression of being a boy scout` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sought to enforce or exercise authority by virtue of the item` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the by-laws or rules authorise that authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `formed, organised, worked with or was concerned in a body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body claims to be boy scouts or connected with the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body has due authority under the Royal Charter` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2 -- who is a boy scout`

-- s 2: "'Association' means the Boy Scouts Association incorporated under the Royal Charter granted on 4 January 1912"; "'boy scout'
-- means a boy scout recognised as such under the constitution, by-laws or rules of the Association, and includes also all officers of
-- the Association."
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a boy scout` IF
        `the person`'s `is recognised as a boy scout under the Association's rules`
    OR  `the person`'s `is an officer of the Association`

-- ss 3 and 4 speak of a badge, token or emblem "specifically adopted for use by boy scouts under the by-laws or rules of the
-- Association". Only s 5 adds a badge "purporting or appearing to be such".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is a real or apparent Association badge` IF
        `the person`'s `the item is a badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for boy scouts`
    OR  `the person`'s `the item only purports or appears to be an Association badge`

§§ `3 -- selling badges`

-- s 3: "No person, other than the Association, shall sell or expose for sale any badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for use by
-- boy scouts under the by-laws or rules of the Association."
--
-- The only person excepted is the Association. Being a boy scout or an officer is no exception, and the text draws no line between new
-- and second-hand badges.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 3` IF
        `the person`'s `sold or exposed for sale the item`
    AND `the person`'s `the item is a badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for boy scouts`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is the Association itself`)

§§ `4 -- wearing badges without being a scout`

-- s 4: "No person, not being a boy scout, shall publicly wear, carry or bear in such a manner as to convey the impression that he is a
-- boy scout, any badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for use by boy scouts under the by-laws or rules of the Association."
--
-- Four things together: not a boy scout, publicly, an adopted badge, and a manner that conveys the impression of being a scout.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 4` IF
        (NOT `is a boy scout` `the person`)
    AND `the person`'s `publicly wore, carried or bore the item`
    AND `the person`'s `in a manner conveying the impression of being a boy scout`
    AND `the person`'s `the item is a badge, token or emblem specifically adopted for boy scouts`

§§ `5 -- a scout exercising authority by the badge`

-- s 5: "No boy scout shall seek or attempt, by virtue of his wearing, carrying or bearing any badge, token or emblem of the Association,
-- or badge, token or emblem purporting or appearing to be such, to enforce or exercise authority otherwise than in accordance with and
-- as authorised by the by-laws or rules of the Association."
--
-- Only a boy scout (officers included) can contravene s 5. Seeking or attempting is enough; the authority need not be obtained.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 5` IF
        `is a boy scout` `the person`
    AND `the item is a real or apparent Association badge` `the person`
    AND `the person`'s `sought to enforce or exercise authority by virtue of the item`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `the by-laws or rules authorise that authority`)

§§ `6 -- unauthorised "boy scouts" bodies`

-- s 6: "No person shall form, organise, or work in connection with, or be concerned in forming, organising, or working in connection
-- with, any corps or body which without due authority granted under the Royal Charter of the Association claims or purports to be
-- 'boy scouts', or otherwise to be connected with the Association."
--
-- Claiming the name "boy scouts" is enough; the body need not also claim a link with the Association.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 6` IF
        `the person`'s `formed, organised, worked with or was concerned in a body`
    AND `the person`'s `the body claims to be boy scouts or connected with the Association`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `the body has due authority under the Royal Charter`)

§§ `7 -- penalty`

-- s 7: "Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of this Act shall be guilty of an offence, and on summary conviction thereof
-- before a Magistrate's Court shall be liable to a fine not exceeding $200."
--
-- A fine only: s 7 provides no imprisonment.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits an offence under s 7` IF
        `contravenes s 3` `the person`
    OR  `contravenes s 4` `the person`
    OR  `contravenes s 5` `the person`
    OR  `contravenes s 6` `the person`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    IF `commits an offence under s 7` `the person` THEN 200 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the person` IS A Conduct, `fine imposed` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within s 7` IF
        `commits an offence under s 7` `the person`
    AND `fine imposed` <= 200
    AND `months of imprisonment imposed` EQUALS 0
